we have finally seen some gameplay of  halo infinite  despite some grumbling about the visuals  it's looking like a pretty good halo  game  there's a lot of details in the 8 minute  demo some  obvious and others more subtle in this  video we've gone ahead and compiled all  of that information  for you into one super video let's get  to it  let's start with the story the opening  of the demo sets the time frame on may  28th  2560 160  days after we lost this event is  referred to  several times but the game is staying  cagey on what exactly this  is for reference the events of halo 5  take place and  end in october of 2558  and the events of halo wars 2 take place  in 2559  343 has stated that infinite is set to  be the conclusion  of the forerunner saga the storyline  that started all the way back in halo 4.  it's also going to set the path for  future halo stories  the main villains of the game are the  banished a splinter group that broke off  from the covenant long ago  they were the main antagonists of halo  wars 2 and  no you do not need to play that game in  order to understand the story of  infinite according to 343  the leader of the banished and infinite  is warchief as  char charm as charm and go ahead and say  that  he has taken over the banished in  replace of atriox the villain from halo  wars 2.  he and his banished have taken control  of a halo ring presumably installation  0-4 the ring from combat evolved  and is seemingly trying to repair it in  his big speech at the end of the demo  he mentioned the harbinger someone who  shares the same goal as the banished  we don't know who this is and 343 isn't  telling  but come on probably cortana last thing  of note i thought was interesting  is ign asked 343 how much master chief  talks in this one  and the answer was somewhere in between  the mostly silent chief of the original  trilogy  wait here and the very chatty chief of  halo 4  and 5. let's talk how halo infinite is  structured because it's by far the most  intriguing aspect  and also still the least clear 343 has  said the game still has a story  progression of a beginning a middle  and an end within the game there are  these large open spaces which have  optional missions and  places to explore how much of the game  is  like this is unclear they have stated  that you can return to previous areas to  explore places you missed though  as a part of this new open level design  343 has stated that the game is  several times larger than our last two  campaigns put together  which will make it the largest halo game  to date  to help navigate these large  environments is the brand new map  in it you can do basic map stuff like  set waypoints and  check which missions are available you  know basic video game things  in gameplay chief has a scan pulse  ability which shows nearby objects of  interest and objectives  interestingly these appear to have a  difficulty associated with them  in this objective to take out gun  battery west you can see the symbol the  franchise traditionally uses for  normal difficulty in the menu we also  see an  upgrade tab but we don't actually get to  see what it looks like  343 has stated that the upgrades are  referring to the new equipment master  chief picks up over the game  they assure players that there is no  experience meter or experience based  skill tree  speaking of equipment the demo featured  what is probably the biggest change to  master chief's arsenal  a grappling hook known as the grapple  shot  it seems to be a pretty versatile piece  of equipment letting you close the gap  on enemies traverse the environment  and pick up objects like fusion coils  that you can then throw  i'm super curious if you can use this to  pick up weapons off the ground  the other equipment shown is the drop  wall a front-facing energy wall that  functions a lot like halo 3's bubble  shield  except that chief can shoot through his  side equipment like the drop wall appear  to be a one-time use while the grapple  shot has a cooldown  let's round it out by getting super  specific and talking weapons  on the unsc side we got the brand new vk  78 commando a full auto machine gun with  a scope that's described as  good for mid long range this seems to  fill the role usually meant for  something like the battle rifle  but don't worry that gun also is making  a return  we see it for half a second in the  trailer and its design is in line with  the classic halo 2 look  we also have the cqs48 bulldog  a 12 gauge riot shotgun that is  apparently replacing the classic halo  shotgun  of course the assault rifle returns  sporting a look closer in design to the  version seen in halo reach  this one is the ma40ar while the reach  one was the ma37  so it does indeed appear to be an  upgrade from the original the pistol  shown is the mk50 sidekick which gives  off strong halo 2 vibes and  doesn't appear to have a scope in fact  it's worth pointing out that we don't  see  any aiming down sights on weapons that  don't have scopes  so it seems that 343 has gone back on  the design decision  to give all weapons ads like they did in  halo 5.  on the covenant side there's the pulse  carbine a new weapon that seems like a  fusion of the plasma rifle and the  covenant carbine  the plasma pistols there but we don't  get to see in action and there's a brief  look at the energy sword in a new  trailer  the return of brutes means the return of  brute weapons like the spike grenade  there's the mangler a slow but powerful  pistol that reminds me a lot of the  mauler shotgun from halo 3.  and last there is the ravanger a new  three round burst weapon that is energy  based with a percent meter  and vent forward loading 343 has said  that banished weapons with blades on  them  will do more melee damage than typical  melee the game will run at 60fps  although 343 has only been referring to  the series x when talking about it  so we're not really sure if it'll reach  that on say the standard xbox one  it will also run up to 4k on the series  x  they've also stated that next gen  features like ray tracing will be coming  post launch as a free  update now the demo has been getting  some flack for its visuals  xbox marketing general manager aaron  greenberg has said in an interview with  inside gaming  that the game is still a work in  progress and is confident the game will  continue to get  better and better in the coming months  they've also confirmed a pc version  like with the master chief collection  you can get it on windows 10 the xbox  game pass app and yes  even steam 343 has said there is a  dedicated team focusing on the pc  version  in order to make sure it's the best it  can possibly be  343 is saving a big multiplayer reveal  for later on but we did get a few  tidbits  after the backlash from halo 5's lack of  split screen  343 has confirmed that infinite will  feature two-player split screen  co-op on the pvp end the grapple shot  will show up but as a pickup  not a permanent ability also there was a  rumor that the game wouldn't launch with  multiplayer  but that has been confirmed as false  however if you were hoping for a public  beta  which was originally planned 343 has  gone back on that  and can't make any promises and finally  343 has said that halo infinite  is a platform for the future of the  series but  what exactly does that mean instead of  another box sequel future halo stories  will be added onto infinite  and they've built the game and their  tech around this idea  343 has stressed that halo infinite  isn't a live service game like destiny  and this idea is more like how they've  been continually adding to the master  chief collection over the years  and that is every little detail we now  know of halo infinite  the game is scheduled for a fall release  with the xbox series x  which is coming up really fast expect a  lot more details on halo infinite in the  coming months  so come back to gamespot for all the  latest information thanks for watching  you
 

